    <h3>Advanced Prompting Patterns</h3>

    <p><strong>Tree of Thoughts (ToT):</strong> Explore multiple reasoning branches like a search tree</p>

    <pre><code>Process:
1. Generate multiple next steps (thought branches)
2. Evaluate each branch's promise
3. Explore most promising branches further
4. Backtrack if branch leads to dead end
5. Find best path to solution

Use case: Creative writing, game playing, complex planning
Performance: Solves problems impossible with linear CoT
Cost: 10-100x more compute than standard CoT</code></pre>

    <p><strong>ReAct (Reasoning + Acting):</strong> Interleave thinking with actions/tool use</p>

    <pre><code>Example:
Thought: I need to find the current temperature in Tokyo
Action: search("current temperature Tokyo")
Observation: 18°C, partly cloudy
Thought: Now I need to compare with New York
Action: search("current temperature New York")
Observation: 22°C, sunny
Thought: New York is warmer
Answer: New York is 4°C warmer than Tokyo

Benefits:
• Breaks down complex tasks requiring external information
• Enables tool use (search, calculator, APIs)
• Self-corrects based on observations
• Foundation for AI agents</code></pre>

    <p><strong>Self-Ask:</strong> Model asks and answers sub-questions</p>

    <pre><code>Question: "Who was president when the iPhone was released?"

Model output:
"Are follow-up questions needed? Yes.
Follow-up: When was the iPhone released?
Intermediate answer: June 2007
Follow-up: Who was US president in June 2007?
Intermediate answer: George W. Bush
Final answer: George W. Bush was president when iPhone was released."</code></pre>

    <div class="callout info">
      <div class="callout-title">💡 Prompting Best Practices (2024)</div>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Start simple:</strong> Try zero-shot before adding examples</li>
        <li><strong>Add CoT for reasoning:</strong> "Let's think step by step" for complex tasks</li>
        <li><strong>Use examples strategically:</strong> 2-3 diverse examples often sufficient</li>
        <li><strong>Be specific:</strong> Clear instructions > vague requests</li>
        <li><strong>Iterate:</strong> Refine prompts based on outputs</li>
        <li><strong>Use system prompts:</strong> Set consistent behavior/tone</li>
        <li><strong>Consider cost:</strong> CoT uses more tokens (balance quality vs. cost)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

