          <td>~96K words</td>
          <td>Open-source long context</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Gemini 1.5 Pro (2024)</strong></td>
          <td><strong>1-2M tokens</strong></td>
          <td><strong>~750K-1.5M words</strong></td>
          <td><strong>Entire codebases, hours of video</strong></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Gemini 1.5 Flash (2024)</strong></td>
          <td><strong>1M tokens</strong></td>
          <td><strong>~750K words</strong></td>
          <td><strong>Fast long-context processing</strong></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>What Long Context Enables</h3>

    <p><strong>1M+ tokens unlocks entirely new capabilities:</strong></p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Entire Codebases:</strong> Analyze 10,000+ file repositories in one context</li>
      <li><strong>Full Books:</strong> Process complete novels, textbooks, technical manuals</li>
      <li><strong>Video Analysis:</strong> 1 hour of video = ~700K tokens (Gemini multimodal)</li>
      <li><strong>Multi-Document Reasoning:</strong> Compare/synthesize across dozens of papers</li>
      <li><strong>Extended Conversations:</strong> Days of chat history without losing context</li>
      <li><strong>Complex System Understanding:</strong> Map entire software architectures</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Technical Challenges Solved</h3>

    <pre><code>Key Innovations Enabling Long Context:

1. Efficient Attention Mechanisms:
   • Flash Attention: 2-4x faster, less memory
   • Grouped Query Attention (GQA): Reduces KV cache
   • Sparse Attention: Attend to relevant tokens only

2. Position Encoding Improvements:
   • RoPE (Rotary Position Embeddings): Better extrapolation
   • ALiBi: Attention with Linear Biases
   • Learned absolute positions with interpolation

3. KV Cache Optimization:
   • Compression techniques
   • Quantization (INT8/INT4)
   • Selective token retention

4. Training Strategies:
   • Long-context fine-tuning on extended sequences
   • Curriculum learning (short → long)
   • Synthetic long-context data generation</code></pre>

    <div class="callout warning">
      <div class="callout-title">⚠️ Long Context Considerations</div>
      <p><strong>Challenges remain even with 1M+ context:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>"Lost in the Middle":</strong> Models may miss info buried in long contexts</li>
        <li><strong>Cost:</strong> Longer context = more compute = higher API costs</li>
        <li><strong>Latency:</strong> Processing 1M tokens takes time (seconds to minutes)</li>
        <li><strong>Quality varies:</strong> Not all positions attended equally well</li>
        <li><strong>Retrieval still helps:</strong> RAG can be more efficient than full context</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Best practice:</strong> Use long context when needed, but consider retrieval
      (RAG) for efficiency when dealing with massive knowledge bases.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Limitations and Challenges</h2>

    <div class="callout warning">
      <div class="callout-title">⚠️ Known Issues</div>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Hallucinations:</strong> Generate plausible but false information</li>
        <li><strong>Lack of grounding:</strong> No connection to real-world facts</li>
        <li><strong>Reasoning limitations:</strong> Struggle with complex logic and math</li>
        <li><strong>Outdated knowledge:</strong> Training data has cutoff date</li>
        <li><strong>Inconsistency:</strong> Different responses to same question</li>
        <li><strong>Bias:</strong> Reflect biases in training data</li>
        <li><strong>No true understanding:</strong> Pattern matching, not comprehension</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>Best Practices</h2>

    <div class="callout success">
      <div class="callout-title">✅ Effective LLM Usage</div>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Clear instructions:</strong> Be specific and unambiguous</li>
        <li><strong>Provide context:</strong> Include relevant background information</li>
        <li><strong>Use examples:</strong> Few-shot prompting improves performance</li>
        <li><strong>Break down tasks:</strong> Decompose complex problems</li>
        <li><strong>Verify outputs:</strong> Always fact-check critical information</li>
        <li><strong>Iterate prompts:</strong> Refine based on responses</li>
        <li><strong>Set temperature:</strong> Lower for factual, higher for creative</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>Summary</h2>

    <p>Large Language Models represent a paradigm shift in AI, achieving remarkable capabilities through scale and sophisticated training. Key points:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Built on Transformer architecture, scaled to billions/trillions of parameters</li>
      <li>Three-phase training: pre-training, SFT, RLHF</li>
      <li>Emergent abilities appear only at sufficient scale</li>
      <li>Effective prompting is critical for good results</li>
      <li>Still have significant limitations (hallucinations, reasoning, grounding)</li>
    </ul>

